      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To address Tupper's comment on the developer stream directly ( https://www.twitch.tv/videos/2750638358?t=01h31m43s >\"...or lessen the security capabilities of eac on virtual machines which we also cannot do\" )\n\nthe current method to play on *any* virtual machine solution is to spoof many devices in the system to appear as real hardware via hacks and patches. This is not a \"security\" thing VMs get wrong, this is simply necessary evasion when an application is trying to block the execution in virtual machines. I am still very much interested in a direct addressing of whether or not VRC can simply no longer try to detect and block VMs.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
